From: Jeremy Rose <nornagon@nornagon.net>
Subject: [PATCH] Use supported Emscripten macro in input handling

The upstream input wait refactor added two more platform guards using the
deprecated EMSCRIPTEN macro. Use __EMSCRIPTEN__ so Emscripten 6.0.8 can
compile with warnings treated as errors.

diff --git a/src/sdltiles.cpp b/src/sdltiles.cpp
--- a/src/sdltiles.cpp
+++ b/src/sdltiles.cpp
@@ -6557,7 +6557,7 @@
 
 // This is how we're actually going to handle input events, SDL getch
 // is simply a wrapper around this.
-#if !defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
+#if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
 // time until next android touch timer CheckMessages checks, from its file statics
 static std::optional<uint32_t> android_touch_wait_ms( const uint32_t now )
 {
@@ -6637,7 +6637,7 @@
         try_sdl_update();
     }
 
-#if defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
     // emscripten must yield to the browser through Asyncify, which SDL_Delay does
     if( inputdelay < 0 ) {
         do {
